            <ArticleTitle>Peroneal tendoscopy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-25</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fcl.2014.10.011</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1083-7515(14)00131-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Peroneal tendoscopy is indicated for peroneal tenosynovitis, subluxation or dislocation, snapping, partial tears requiring debridement, and postoperative adhesions and scarring. Peroneal tendoscopy was also found to be valuable as a diagnostic tool in some instances. It is generally reported to have good to excellent outcomes in most patients with a relatively low occurrence of complications.</AbstractText>
